     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "'Here is a post from the social network VKontakte. Your task is to determine whether the post expresses value.  You will answer the question: Does the post reflect the importance of any object,  phenomenon, or process?  Choose one of four categories: Yes, it does; No, it does not; Unclear; Spam. Values are a person's belief in the importance of an object, phenomenon, or quality. Select Yes, it does if the text represents: The importance of romantic relationships, love, fidelity, friendship, devotion to loved ones (including love for children);  The importance of equality for all people or the preservation of nature;  The desire for stability and order, following rules, the importance of safety, the need to take care of one's health;  The importance of being independent, the desire to try new things, to take risks;  The importance of achieving goals, receiving well-deserved rewards;  The importance of simply enjoying life.  Please keep in mind that other types of values may also appear in the texts—take your own understanding into account! Also, keep in mind that a text reflecting a value may: not directly mention a particular value; express a denial of a value (these should also be marked as Yes, reflects).  Examples of texts reflecting values: “People are always critical. Don't let them break you. Achieving your goal is the best form of revenge” - an example of an implicit reference to the importance of achieving your goals. “Murphy's Law is the only law that works in our country!” - an example of an implicit reference to the importance of following the rules. “This is truly one of the best days of our lives! Thank you, my dear” - an example of reflecting the value of love. “Sometimes you have to treat yourself #cakes #ice cream #eating” - an example of reflecting the value of pleasure. Select: No, it does not reflect if:  The text does not reflect the importance of any object or value. For example:  Standard congratulations, recipes (culinary or other), without personal evaluation;  Emotional statements that do not indicate the importance or value of anything  Examples of texts that do not reflect values: "How touching! I almost cried!“ or  ”Oh, how lovely🤣“ - the subject of the statement is unclear. ”Thank you all for your congratulations!“ or ”New Year 2015" - routine thanks and congratulations. Select Unclear if: you are looking at a text that is difficult to understand due to the use of unfamiliar names, words, places, or an unclear context.  Select Spam if:  Texts written for advertising purposes, including on behalf of organizations. Types of spam:  advertisements for the sale of goods and services;  requests to subscribe to someone;  requests to click on a link;  and other advertising posts, including those with veiled advertising. Examples of spam texts: "Direct flights from Perm to Min. Vody  226-57-06“ - a clear advertisement for sale ”IF YOU WANT TO MOVE FORWARD - YOU NEED TO LEARN!!!! And do it with energetic people who are full of positive emotions, who are crazy about their work and are ready to share their knowledge and experience... <...> #depilationorel #learningfromthebest" - hidden advertising Select one of four categories as your answer: Yes, it does; No, it doesn't; Not sure; Spam.'"
      ]
     },
